  era: "1848\u20131856 \xB7 Section 19 \xB7 British Expansion \xB7 1757 \u2013 1856"
  title: Doctrine of Lapse
  text: Under Lord Dalhousie, from 1848 to 1856, a dependent state whose ruler died without a natural heir would lapse to the British; adopted sons were not recognised. Satara, Jhansi and Nagpur were annexed this way.
